diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1437d33
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,137 @@
+# Quizzy
+
+A local Rust/SQLite application for preparing and playing live conference quizzes.
+
+## Run
+
+From the project root:
+
+```sh
+export PORT=3000
+export SECRET_KEY_BASE='a-long-random-secret'
+export QUIZZY_MODERATOR_USERNAME='moderator'
+export QUIZZY_MODERATOR_PASSWORD='choose-a-password'
+bin/serve
+```
+
+`bin/serve` builds the locked dependencies in release mode **offline**, creates
+`storage/`, and runs in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:$PORT`. Database tables are
+initialized automatically. `/up` is public; `/moderate` and every route below
+it require HTTP Basic authentication. The app serves plain HTTP, accepts any
+host name, and has no external service dependencies.
+
+All persistent application data is in `storage/quizzy.sqlite3` (including SQLite
+WAL/SHM companion files). Keep this directory across restarts. For a simple
+backup, stop the app and copy `storage/`. Credentials and the secret are read
+from the environment, never stored in the database. Set the same secret on
+restarts; changing it invalidates already-open forms.
+
+HTTP Basic credentials are not encrypted over plain HTTP. Use the app on a
+trusted/private conference network.
+
+## Play a live game
+
+Prepare a quiz in `/moderate`, then choose **Start a game**. Each click creates
+an independent game and opens its moderator big screen. Share the full join URL
+or display its locally generated QR code. Players enter **Your name** and press
+**Join**; no account is needed. Their browser remembers them for that game.
+
+Use **Start**, **Finish**, **Next**, and finally **End quiz**. Phones and counters
+update live without reloads. Players can change their selection until **Finish**;
+only their last selection counts. Correct answers are never sent to players
+before the question closes. Late joining is allowed until the game ends.
+
+Only active questions are copied into a game, in quiz order. Quiz edits do not
+change games already created. A **Games** list on the quiz page lets moderators
+return to an existing big screen after a restart. Game state, players, and
+answers persist in SQLite. An empty game ends safely when started.
+
+Active-player counts use live connections and heartbeat leases, with a short
+Wi-Fi reconnection grace period; closed tabs are removed after about 8–10 seconds,
+and silently unreachable devices expire after at most 35–37 seconds. Rejoining
+restores the same player and their answers. [Protocol/design notes](docs/live-games.md).
+
+## Scores and prizes
+
+In **Settings**, choose **Number of winners** (a positive whole number, default
+3). Each new game snapshots that setting along with its questions.
+
+Correct final answers earn one point. Equal scores are ranked by the sum of
+elapsed times on correct answers, measured from each question opening to the
+last accepted pick. Players never see running points. Questions are pushed
+immediately to the screen and phones over server-sent events.
+
+After **End quiz**, the screen shows every player in place order with their
+points, and each phone shows its own place and points. Use:
+
+- **Top N** (for example **Top 3**) to award the first N positive-scoring players.
+- **Draw** to award everyone above the N-th score and randomly fill the remaining
+  prizes from everyone tied on that score, ignoring speed. Each click draws anew;
+  a random draw can legitimately repeat the previous selection.
+- **Reset winners** to clear all awards.
+
+Zero-point players never win. If fewer than N players score, they all win.
+**Winner** marks on the screen and **You won!** on phones update live, including
+after reconnection or reopening the page. Scores, timing, and winners survive
+server restarts. [Scoring/prize design notes](docs/prizes.md).
+
+## Reuse and share quizzes
+
+On a quiz page, choose **Export** and copy the JSON. On `/moderate`, choose
+**Import quiz**, paste it into **Quiz JSON**, and press **Import**. This always
+creates a separate quiz, even with a matching title. Invalid JSON or questions
+show errors without saving any part of the quiz. [Format and validation notes](docs/quiz-transfers.md).
+
+## Test
+
+Dependencies are downloaded and both debug and release builds have been built.
+For a fresh development environment with crates.io access, first use `cargo fetch`.
+
+```sh
+cargo test --offline --locked
+cargo clippy --offline --locked --all-targets -- -D warnings
+```
+
+With a running app, export its moderator credentials and run:
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/smoke.py
+python3 tests/transfer.py
+python3 tests/transfer_browser.py
+python3 tests/browser.py
+python3 tests/live.py
+python3 tests/live_browser.py
+python3 tests/prizes.py
+python3 tests/prizes_browser.py
+python3 tests/prizes_persistence.py setup
+python3 tests/live_persistence.py setup
+python3 tests/persistence.py setup
+# Stop and restart bin/serve with the same environment.
+python3 tests/live_persistence.py verify
+python3 tests/prizes_persistence.py verify
+python3 tests/persistence.py verify
+```
+
+Tests use Python's standard library; the browser test uses installed Chromium,
+not any downloaded browser automation package. Fixtures are cleaned up, and
+browser screenshots/logs are written under ignored `storage/`. `TEST_URL` can
+override the default `http://127.0.0.1:3000` for HTTP/browser tests.
+
+## Question timer
+
+Set **Timer minutes** and **Timer seconds** in **Quiz settings**. Both default to
+0; 0 minutes and 0 seconds disables the timer. The moderator sees an M:SS
+countdown while a question is open; players never see it. Expiry behaves like
+**Finish**, which also remains available early. **Next** starts a fresh timer.
+Deadlines survive reloads and restarts, and the server handles expiry even when
+no moderator browser is connected. Each game snapshots the quiz's timer setting.
+Timers are local settings, not exported content; imported quizzes have no timer.
+
+Timer regressions (the first two run against `bin/serve`; the restart test launches
+an isolated release binary and temporary database):
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/timer.py
+python3 tests/timer_browser.py
+python3 tests/timer_persistence.py
+```
